# Can we also check audio and video check in the system requirement feature, why there is 2 different ways of checking the system
## [~accountid:712020:46a94ac2-794d-40e3-9e05-ed691c2178d4] {color:#ff5630}Its already there now.{color}
# Can we also show the working of each new feature inside the employer portal itself
## For eg; we can give a link saying “Watch tutorial“ or “Watch working“ something similar for “AI insight“ or other features on the tooltip
### [~accountid:712020:46a94ac2-794d-40e3-9e05-ed691c2178d4]{color:#ff5630} we had this implemented for Create assessment flow, later we discontinued as Helpscout doesn’t have this feature.{color}
## For each question type we can embed the youtube video on the bottom right which explain the working and how the question will look for a candidate, so the employer not have to goo through the preview for each question which is time consuming if i have added multiple questions
### [~accountid:712020:46a94ac2-794d-40e3-9e05-ed691c2178d4]{color:#36b37e} This is doable.{color}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
On the candidate side we need to show recorded video just like audio/video question
{panel}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
h1. Major points:

# We can add a “Case Studies” section showing how we fulfill requirements for each customer.
# Use actual workflows in the form of GIFs wherever possible.
# Focus on benefits and data-driven content: instead of just listing features, highlight outcomes such as reduced time-to-hire, lower turnover, and improved candidate experience. For example: “95%+ of candidates rated their experience as positive.”
{panel}

----

h1. A) UX point of view:

# Navigation and information architecture
## {color:#36b37e}The top navigation is short and not overloaded{color}
## {color:#36b37e}Clear sectioning on the homepage{color}
## {color:#ff5630}“Get Started” is vague, does it mean demo booking, free trial, or contact sales?{color}
## {color:#ff5630}The navigation doesn’t adapt much to different user intents (HR leaders, recruiters, candidates, IT/security), users with different goals might struggle to know where to go{color}

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
Suggestion: Use something like “Book a demo”
{panel}

----

h1. B) UI Solution for Testlify as per MakiPeople

# We can tailor navigation based on each user’s use case. The system should ask for their industry and requirements, then show a customized page highlighting how we serve that industry (all clients, problems solved, and results) Other industries and use cases can be moved to the footer or offered as filters on the solutions page
!image-20250929-065454.png|width=97.12230215827337%,alt="image-20250929-065454.png"!

# Homepage: Hero section
## {color:#36b37e}The headline is large, bold and readable, it establishes hierarchy immediately, good visual signal that orients the eye to the proposition first{color}
## {color:#36b37e}Clean whitespace around the hero copy gives breathing room and focus to the CTA{color}
## {color:#ff5630}As s SaaS product, visitors often expect a screenshot or short animation that shows the product in action{color}
## {color:#ff5630}On smaller screens the hero likely pushes the CTA well below the fold{color}
# Homepage: Trusted Logos / Social Proof Strip
## {color:#36b37e}High-profile logos (Nespresso, Capgemini, H&M etc…){color}
# Homepage: “Build one-of-a-kind HR agents” section
## {color:#ff5630}There’s no quick diagram showing how you go from “agent builder” to live candidate interaction{color}
## {color:#ff5630}The text lists channels (phone, SMS, web) but doesn’t show the candidate experience{color}
# Homepage: Features grid (Screening, Interview scheduling, Interviewing, Sourcing, Assessment)
## {color:#36b37e}Feature headings are grouped logically (screening → interviewing → selection) which matches recruiter mental models.{color}
# Homepage: Impact / Metrics
## {color:#36b37e}Metrics (80% automation, 2–3x reduction in time-to-hire, etc.) are compelling and placed prominently, powerful for decision-makers{color}
## {color:#ff5630}No immediate links to the case studies that back each metric from this area — metrics without quick evidence lower credibility{color}
# Homepage: Integrations block (Workday, SAP, ATS logos)
## {color:#36b37e}Highlighting Workday / SAP and other ATSs immediately reassures technical stakeholders{color}
## {color:#ff5630}Mobile view could collapse logos awkwardly without a way to see which logos are included{color}
# Homepage: Trust and security section
## {color:#36b37e}ISO 27001, end-to-end encryption, excellent for enterprise & security teams. {color}
# Product page: Screening hero & product details
# Product page: Immersive role simulations
# Customers page: 
## {color:#36b37e}Case studies are present and include outcomes{color}
## {color:#ff5630}Case studies lack consistent structure (problem > solution > results){color}
## {color:#ff5630}It would be great if I could view the case studies by filter, especially when I want to check a specific domain (e.g., Retail, Finance){color}
# Resources page: 
## {color:#ff5630}The page lacks filters, the data is open (e.g; if i want to see specific to design, then ill have to scroll and search){color}
{color:#36b37e}Add a “Suggested for you” strip based on the page you visited (if they land from Product → suggest Product case studies).{color}
# Footer & Utility links
## {color:#36b37e}All legal and social links are present good completeness and visual location at the bottom.{color}

----

